<title>MEXICO: Mexico's June preliminary trade surplus $182 mln.</title>
<headline>Mexico's June preliminary trade surplus $182 mln.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's preliminary trade surplus for June was $182 million, the Finance Ministry said in a statement on Wednesday.</p>
<p>It said that exports in June were $9.229 billion, while imports were $9.047 billion.  </p>
<p>A survey of 13 brokerages and research firms by Reuters had found expectations of a surplus of $164 million in the month.</p>
<p>The Finance Ministry said that the trade surplus for the first six months of the year was $1.965 billion.</p>
